---
// Static figure: where a Maya lintel was, and where it is now. Left, a section through a doorway (the stone wall with
// its opening, the lintel spanning the top of the opening, its carved underside marked): the carved slab spans
// the opening with its carving facing down, so a visitor sees it only from inside the doorway, looking up (after the
// Metropolitan Museum's account of the La Pasadita lintel). Right, the same slab as it is shown in a museum, upright on
// a wall. Simple drawings of relationships, not a reconstruction of the La Pasadita building. Uses the step layout of
// the stained-glass figure, in two columns.
---
<figure class="glass-steps two">
  <ol>
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 160 110" aria-hidden="true">
        <path class="lv-stone" d="M14 0 H146 V104 H106 V40 H54 V104 H14 Z" />
        <path class="lv-slab" d="M46 30 H114 V40 H46 Z" />
        <path class="lv-carve" d="M54 40 H106" />
        <circle class="lv-person" cx="80" cy="70" r="5" />
        <path class="lv-person-line" d="M80 75 V92 M80 92 L74 104 M80 92 L86 104 M80 81 L72 88 M80 81 L88 88" />
        <path class="lv-sight" d="M82 65 L92 42" />
        <path class="lv-ground" d="M0 104 H160" />
      </svg>
      <p><strong>原来：平放在门道顶上</strong>浮雕门楣横架在门洞上方，刻面朝下。只有走进门道、抬起头，才看得见；光线昏暗时，也许还要借助火把。</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 160 110" aria-hidden="true">
        <path class="lv-wall" d="M10 4 H150 V104 H10 Z" />
        <path class="lv-slab" d="M58 22 H102 V72 H58 Z" />
        <path class="lv-relief" d="M64 30 H96 M64 30 V64 M72 40 Q78 34 84 40 Q80 48 72 46 Z M86 50 H96 V64 H86 Z M66 56 H80" />
        <circle class="lv-person" cx="122" cy="66" r="5" />
        <path class="lv-person-line" d="M122 71 V92 M122 92 L116 104 M122 92 L128 104 M122 78 L114 86 M122 78 L130 86" />
        <path class="lv-sight" d="M117 64 L104 52" />
        <path class="lv-ground" d="M0 104 H160" />
      </svg>
      <p><strong>今天：竖立在博物馆的墙上</strong>同一块石头被取下、竖起来，与视线齐平，灯光从正面照亮。看起来更清楚，但原来抬头仰望的观看方式已经消失了。</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <figcaption>示意图：门楣原来的位置与今天的陈列方式，依据大都会艺术博物馆对这块门楣的说明绘制；建筑比例与人物均为示意，不是对拉帕萨迪塔建筑的复原。</figcaption>
</figure>
